  "boundary":"This programme discovers FDA 510(k) submission/decision records with K/BK identifiers. Substantial-equivalence semantics are recognized only for the exact FDA-documented decision-code allowlist. Record presence, descriptions, device names or applicant data do not independently create a clearance claim. Even a substantially-equivalent/cleared record does not establish PMA approval, global authorization, complete clinical effectiveness, exact identity of every commercial configuration, system-wide conformance, automatic assessment reopening, or UNESCO/institutional endorsement. DEN-prefixed De Novo records are explicitly out of scope for v0.1 and require a separate programme."
